    "Weak regret: per-round loss is min of the two selected arms' losses",
    "Outcome matrices M^t in {-1,1} (skew-symmetric) fixed by the adversary; per-round Borda loss ell_t^i = 1/2 + (1/(2K)) sum_j M^t_{ji}; outcome observed is M^t_{A_t B_t}"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "In the non-stochastic setting, this leads to the following definition of loss vectors \\bm \\ell_t: \\ell_t^i = \\frac 1 K \\sum_{j=1}^K \\frac{M_{ji}^t + 1}{2} = \\frac 1 2 + \\frac 1 {2 K} \\sum_{j=1}^K M_{ji}^t. ... The Borda winner is an action minimising the cumulative Borda loss"
  }
